</math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">A solution to the given system of equations is&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where&nbsp;<math alttext="x greater than 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["6"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext="y equals 4 x"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>4</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math> and <math alttext="y equals x squared minus 12"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>12</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Since <math alttext="y equals 4 x"><mrow>
	<mi>y</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mn>4</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>, substituting <math alttext="4 x"><mrow>
	<mn>4</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the second equation of the given system yields <math alttext="4 x equals x squared minus 12"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>4</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>12</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="4 x"><mrow>
	<mn>4</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext="0 equals x squared minus 4 x minus 12"><mrow>
	<mn>0</mn>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>4</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>12</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext="0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 2 right parenthesis"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext="x minus 6 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>6</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> or <math alttext="x plus 2 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>2</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Adding <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext="x minus 6 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>6</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals 6"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="2"><mn>2</mn>
</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext="x plus 2 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>2</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals negative 2"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, solutions to the given system of equations occur when <math alttext="x equals 6"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>6</mn>
</mrow>
</math> and when <math alttext="x equals negative 2"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a solution to the given system of equations is <math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext="x greater than 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Since <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math> is greater than <math alttext="0"><mn>0</mn>
</math>, it follows that the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="6"><mn>6</mn>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"30a07668","external_id":"bf79b193-f7b7-4f48-a581-1f6665ce3add","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"e8801076-227f-4b4b-b360-b691d1341a20","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A solution to the given system of equations is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x greater than 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["6"],"correct_answer":["6"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, substituting <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the second equation of the given system yields <math alttext=\"4 x equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared minus 4 x minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 2 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext=\"x minus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"x plus 2 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x minus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 2 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, solutions to the given system of equations occur when <math alttext=\"x equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and when <math alttext=\"x equals negative 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a solution to the given system of equations is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext=\"x greater than 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Since <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> is greater than <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, it follows that the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357396,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"30a07668","skill_cd":"P.B.","score_band_range_cd":4,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","createDate":1730147357396,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"bf79b193-f7b7-4f48-a581-1f6665ce3add","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"e8801076-227f-4b4b-b360-b691d1341a20","difficulty":"M"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[],"externalid":"bf79b193-f7b7-4f48-a581-1f6665ce3add","keys":["6"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"y equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Since <math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>, substituting <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> in the second equation of the given system yields <math alttext=\"4 x equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math> from both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"0 equals x squared minus 4 x minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math>. This equation can be rewritten as <math alttext=\"0 equals left parenthesis x minus 6 right parenthesis left parenthesis x plus 2 right parenthesis\"><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. By the zero product property, <math alttext=\"x minus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> or <math alttext=\"x plus 2 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Adding <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> to both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x minus 6 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Subtracting <math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math> from both sides of the equation <math alttext=\"x plus 2 equals 0\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>0</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"x equals negative 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Therefore, solutions to the given system of equations occur when <math alttext=\"x equals 6\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math> and when <math alttext=\"x equals negative 2\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. It&rsquo;s given that a solution to the given system of equations is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where <math alttext=\"x greater than 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Since <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math> is greater than <math alttext=\"0\"><mn>0</mn>\n</math>, it follows that the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math>.</p>","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals 4 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>4</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"y equals x squared minus 12\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>y</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>12</mn>\n\t</mrow>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A solution to the given system of equations is&nbsp;<math alttext=\"left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, where&nbsp;<math alttext=\"x greater than 0\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math>?</p>","type":"spr","correct_answer":["6"]},"createDate":1730147357396,"updateDate":1730147357396}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1730147357396, 1730147357396),
    ($SATQ$3148fe3e$SATQ$, $SATQ$b930ff78-e7c0-4bf0-a4c8-db513178d545$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="x squared plus y plus 10 equals 10"><mrow>
