<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="8 x plus 16 minus y equals 0"><mrow><mn>8</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>
<p style="text-align: left;">The solution to the given system of equations is&nbsp;<math alttext="left parenthesis x comma y right parenthesis"><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ba703417-df75-4344-9583-f44445d86239","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 16\"><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"df894231-ad87-4720-b8fe-593d4a190dec","content":"<p><math alttext=\"negative 4\"><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"57479088-b15e-4b96-86bb-b0fdd98c9b82","content":"<p><math alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"5bb57eb2-3bd4-4bf7-a69e-1b5fe5416729","content":"<p><math alttext=\"8\"><mn>8</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["df894231-ad87-4720-b8fe-593d4a190dec"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is correct. Adding <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> to each side of the second equation in the given system of equations yields <math alttext="8 x plus 16 equals y"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>16</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mi>y</mi>
</mrow>
</math>. Substituting <math alttext="8 x plus 16"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>8</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>+</mo>
	<mn>16</mn>
</mrow>
</math> for <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> in the first equation yields <math alttext="x squared plus 8 x plus 16 plus 10 equals 10"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></math>. Subtracting <math alttext="10"><mn>10</mn>
</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext="x squared plus 8 x plus 16 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<msup>
			<mi>x</mi>
			<mn>2</mn>
		</msup>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mrow>
			<mn>8</mn>
			<mi>x</mi>
		</mrow>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>16</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. This&nbsp;equation can be rewritten as <math alttext="left parenthesis x plus 4 right parenthesis squared equals 0"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>. Taking the square root of each side of this equation yields <math alttext="x plus 4 equals 0"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mi>x</mi>
		<mo>+</mo>
		<mn>4</mn>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>0</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Subtracting <math alttext="4"><mn>4</mn>
</math> from each side of this equation yields <math alttext="x equals negative 4"><mrow>
	<mi>x</mi>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mrow>
		<mo>-</mo>
		<mn>4</mn>
	</mrow>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="negative 4"><mrow>
	<mo>-</mo>
	<mn>4</mn>
</mrow>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>, not <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math>.</p>
