$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p class="stem_paragraph ">If one solution to the system of equations above is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_001_7284e904.png" alt="the ordered pair x comma y "></span>, what is one possible value of <span class="italic">x</span> ?</p>
$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["either 8","9"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is either 8 or 9. The first equation can be rewritten as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_002_0984ec24.png" alt="y equals, 17 minus x"></span>. Substituting <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_003_0c7f82fa.png" alt="17 minus x"></span> for <span class="italic">y</span> in the second equation gives <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_004_71c79235.png" alt="x times, open parenthesis, 17 minus x, close parenthesis, equals 72"></span>. By applying the distributive property, this can be rewritten as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_005_f820525a.png" alt="17 x, minus x squared, equals 72"></span>. Subtracting 72 from both sides of the equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_006_023b54ce.png" alt="x squared, minus 17 x, plus 72, equals 0"></span>. Factoring the left-hand side of this equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_007_f7815170.png" alt="open parenthesis, x minus 8, close parenthesis, times, open parenthesis, x minus 9, close parenthesis, equals 0"></span>. Applying the Zero Product Property, it follows that <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_008_aba2202f.png" alt="x minus 8, equals 0"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_009_1dc1b683.png" alt="x minus 9, equals 0"></span>. Solving each equation for <span class="italic">x</span> yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_010_1d4468f6.png" alt="x equals 8"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/364a2d25/img_011_5a3064af.png" alt="x equals 9"></span> respectively. Note that 8 and 9 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
